{
  "name": "threads-poster",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "sticky-readme",
      "name": "Setup Notes",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -260,
        -460
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 660,
        "height": 440,
        "content": "## threads-poster\nWebhook-triggered, per-platform posting workflow for Threads. Credentials come from the request payload only \u2014 never stored in n8n (see websitePlan.md \u00a75).\n\nUnlike Facebook/Instagram, Threads posting is tied directly to the authenticated user's own token (`/me/threads`) \u2014 there's no separate Page/Business ID to pass.\n\n**After importing:** activate the workflow, then:\n\n```bash\ncurl -X POST http://localhost:5678/webhook/threads-poster \\\n  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\n  -d '{\n    \"post_id\": \"pst_test003\",\n    \"user_id\": \"usr_test\",\n    \"platform\": \"threads\",\n    \"content\": \"Test thread #smposting\",\n    \"media_type\": \"TEXT\",\n    \"media_urls\": [],\n    \"token\": { \"access_token\": \"YOUR_THREADS_LONG_LIVED_TOKEN\" },\n    \"callback_url\": \"https://webhook.site/your-id\"\n  }'\n```\n\n`media_type` accepts `TEXT | IMAGE | VIDEO | CAROUSEL`. `TEXT` ignores `media_urls`; `IMAGE`/`VIDEO` need exactly 1 entry; `CAROUSEL` needs 2+ image URLs (image-only for now, matching Facebook/Instagram carousels in this codebase \u2014 Threads' API itself also allows video children, not implemented here).\n\n**Known limitation:** publish uses a blind Wait (5s / 10s / 10s / 60s) instead of polling the container's `status` field until `FINISHED` \u2014 matches the pattern already used for Instagram/the old Threads draft, but Meta's docs recommend polling, especially for video. This is a real gap, not just theoretical: a 1GB video on a slow connection can easily still be `IN_PROGRESS` after 60s, and `threads_publish` will fail with a \"media not ready\" error rather than the wait just being wasted time. Revisit with an actual poll-until-`FINISHED` loop (see status-check pattern below) if video publishes start failing."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "webhook-trigger",
      "name": "Webhook",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.webhook",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        -260,
        0
      ],
      "webhookId": "threads-poster",
      "parameters": {
        "httpMethod": "POST",
        "path": "threads-poster",
        "responseMode": "onReceived",
        "options": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "parse-request",
      "name": "Parse Request",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        -40,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const body = $input.first().json.body || $input.first().json;\nreturn [{\n  json: {\n    post_id: body.post_id,\n    user_id: body.user_id,\n    platform: body.platform || 'threads',\n    content: body.content || '',\n    media_type: String(body.media_type || '').toUpperCase(),\n    media_urls: body.media_urls || [],\n    access_token: body.token && body.token.access_token,\n    callback_url: body.callback_url || 'http://localhost:5000/api/webhooks/n8n-callback'\n  }\n}];"
      }
    },
